<Base title="About"><section class="wrap pagehero"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1>I'm John Cole.</h1><p>A software engineer in Phoenix, Arizona, with a practical interest in building dependable systems and helping people understand technology.</p></section><section class="wrap section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="bodycopy"><p>Since 2012, I've worked independently on software for businesses, often taking responsibility for the full path from understanding the problem to deploying and maintaining the application.</p><p>My work has included web applications, warehouse and auction operations, marketplaces, databases, integrations, and cloud infrastructure. I've worked in Ruby on Rails, Laravel, Python, Go, JavaScript, and other tools depending on what a project needs.</p><p>I completed a BS in Software Engineering at Western Governors University in August 2026 and am working toward an MS in Software Engineering with a DevOps concentration. I'm also exploring opportunities to teach computer science and software development.</p><h2>Experience and tools</h2><p><span class="pill">Ruby on Rails</span><span class="pill">Laravel / PHP</span><span class="pill">Python</span><span class="pill">Go</span><span class="pill">JavaScript</span><span class="pill">Vue</span><span class="pill">React</span><span class="pill">PostgreSQL</span><span class="pill">REST APIs</span><span class="pill">Linux</span><span class="pill">Docker</span><span class="pill">CI/CD</span></p><h2>Get in touch</h2><p>For conversations about software engineering, teaching, or related work, email <a class="textlink" href="mailto:colejd@gmail.com">colejd@gmail.com</a>.</p></div></section></Base>
